## NAMING RULES

Class

PascalCase

ProductController

ProductRepository

ProductService

Method

camelCase

createProduct()

updateStock()

calculateCommission()

Variables

camelCase

$productPrice

$totalAmount

$affiliateUser

Database

snake_case

product_categories

affiliate_commissions

wallet_transactions

Route Names

dot.notation

products.index

products.store

orders.show

------------------------------------------

## CONTROLLER RULES

Controllers must remain thin.

Controllers NEVER contain business logic.

Controllers ONLY

Validate Request

Call Service

Return Resource

Nothing else.

------------------------------------------

## SERVICE RULES

All business logic belongs inside Services.

Examples

ProductService

OrderService

AffiliateService

WalletService

CommissionService

ReportService

Services never return raw arrays.

Services return DTO or Models.

------------------------------------------

## REPOSITORY RULES

Repositories ONLY access database.

Repositories NEVER contain business logic.

Repositories NEVER return JsonResponse.

Repositories NEVER call Request.

------------------------------------------

## MODEL RULES

Models only contain

Relationships

Scopes

Accessors

Mutators

Casting

No business logic.

------------------------------------------

## REQUEST VALIDATION

Always use FormRequest.

Never validate inside Controller.

Always authorize().

Always use custom validation messages.

------------------------------------------

## DATABASE RULES

Every table

timestamps()

softDeletes() where applicable

Foreign Keys

Indexes

Constraints

Always use migration.

Never modify database manually.

------------------------------------------

## RELATIONSHIPS

Always use Eloquent Relationships.

Never write unnecessary joins.

Always eager load relationships.

Avoid N+1 queries.

------------------------------------------

## API RESPONSE

Always use API Resource.

Never return Model directly.

Success Format

{
    "success": true,
    "message": "...",
    "data": {}
}

Error Format

{
    "success": false,
    "message": "...",
    "errors": {}
}

------------------------------------------

## SECURITY

Never trust client input.

Always validate.

Always authorize.

Escape output.

Prevent mass assignment.

Use Policies.

Use Gates.

Protect sensitive routes.

------------------------------------------

## AUTHENTICATION

Laravel Sanctum only.

Never write custom auth.

Use middleware.

Use Policies.

------------------------------------------

## FILE UPLOAD

Always validate mime type.

Always validate size.

Store using Storage.

Never use move_uploaded_file().

Generate unique filenames.

------------------------------------------

## IMAGE HANDLING

Use Intervention Image.

Generate thumbnail.

Optimize image.

Store original.

------------------------------------------

## ERROR HANDLING

Never use dd()

Never use dump()

Never use var_dump()

Use logging.

Throw Exceptions.

Handle exceptions globally.

------------------------------------------

## LOGGING

Use Laravel Log.

Never ignore exceptions.

Log important actions.

Log payment.

Log wallet transaction.

Log commission generation.

------------------------------------------

## QUEUE

Use Queue for

Email

Notification

Commission Calculation

Image Processing

Large Report

------------------------------------------

## CACHE

Use Cache for

Settings

Categories

Permissions

Homepage Data

Never cache user-sensitive data without keys.

------------------------------------------

## TESTING

Write Feature Test.

Write Unit Test.

Test validation.

Test authorization.

Test API.

------------------------------------------

## FRONTEND RULES

Use Vue Composition API.

Use Pinia.

No jQuery.

No inline JavaScript.

Create reusable components.

Never duplicate UI.

------------------------------------------

## TAILWIND

Tailwind only.

No Bootstrap in Frontend.

Responsive first.

Mobile first.

------------------------------------------

## ADMIN PANEL

AdminLTE only.

Do not mix Tailwind inside Admin unless necessary.

------------------------------------------

## GIT

Meaningful commits only.

One feature per commit.

Never commit .env.

Never commit vendor.

Never commit node_modules.

------------------------------------------

## AI INSTRUCTION

Before generating code

1. Analyze existing project.
2. Reuse existing architecture.
3. Never duplicate functionality.
4. Follow existing naming convention.
5. Ask only when information is missing.
6. Generate complete code.
7. Explain only if requested.
8. Prefer maintainability over cleverness.